According to the provided context from 3GPP TS 38.331, when a UE receives an RRCReconfiguration message (or similar configuration) that includes fields in `servingCellConfigCommon` defined in Release 16 or later, but the UE does **not support** those fields, the handling is governed by the general failure behavior for RRC reconfiguration.

Specifically, the relevant clause is:

> **"1 &gt; else if RRCReconfiguration is received via NR (i.e., NR standalone, NE-DC, or NR-DC):**  
> 2 &gt; if the UE is unable to comply with (part of) the configuration included in the RRCReconfiguration message received over SRB3;  
> 3 &gt; if the RRCReconfiguration message was received as part of ConditionalReconfiguration:  
> 4 &gt; continue using the configuration used prior to when the inability to comply with the RRCReconfiguration message was detected;  
> 4 &gt; continue using the configuration used prior to the reception of RRCReconfiguration message;  
> 3 &gt; if MCG transmission is not suspended:  
> 4 &gt; initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration error, upon which the connection reconfiguration procedure ends;  
> 4 &gt; initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in clause 5.3.7, upon which the connection reconfiguration procedure ends;  
> 2 &gt; else if the UE is unable to comply with (part of) the configuration included in the RRCReconfiguration message received over the SRB1 or if the upper layers indicate that the nas-Container is invalid:  
> 3 &gt; if the RRCReconfiguration message was received as part of ConditionalReconfiguration:  
> 4 &gt; continue using the configuration used prior to when the inability to comply with the RRCReconfiguration message was detected;  
> 4 &gt; continue using the configuration used prior to the reception of RRCReconfiguration message;  
> 3 &gt; if AS security has not been activated:  
> 4 &gt; perform the actions upon going to RRC_IDLE as specified in 5.3.11, with release cause 'other';  
> 3 &gt; else if AS security has been activated but SRB

When the UE receives a `condReconfigId` that matches an existing entry in the `condReconfigToAddModList`, and the received entry includes `condRRCReconfig`, the UE **replaces** the existing `condRRCReconfig` within the `VarConditionalReconfig` with the newly received `condRRCReconfig` value.

This behavior is explicitly specified in the first context block:

> 2 > if the entry in condReconfigToAddModList includes an condRRCReconfig;  
> 3 > replace condRRCReconfig within the VarConditionalReconfig with the value received for this condReconfigId;

Thus, the update process is a **direct replacement** of the existing `condRRCReconfig` for the matching `condReconfigId`.

When events associated to all `measId(s)` within `condTriggerConfig` for a target candidate cell are fulfilled, the UE:

- **Considers the target candidate cell within the stored `condRRCReconfig`, associated to that `condReconfigId`, as a triggered cell**;  
- **Initiates the conditional reconfiguration execution**, as specified in **5.3.5.13.5** (or in the referenced clause depending on the context, e.g., TS 36.331 clause 5.3.5.9.5 for EN-DC).

This behavior is explicitly defined in the first context excerpt under the condition:
> 2 > if event(s) associated to all measId(s) within condTriggerConfig for a target candidate cell within the stored condRRCReconfig are fulfilled:  
> 3 > consider the target candidate cell within the stored condRRCReconfig, associated to that condReconfigId, as a triggered cell;  
> 3 > initiate the conditional reconfiguration execution, as specified in 5.3.5.13.5;

Thus, the UE takes the two actions: **marks the cell as triggered** and **starts executing the conditional reconfiguration**.

If the UE receives an **RRCReject** in response to an **RRCResumeRequest** or **RRCResumeRequest1** and the resume was triggered for an **RNA update**, the UE shall:

- **Set the variable `pendingRNA-Update` to `true`**;
- **Discard the current K key, the K key, the K key, the K key, and the K key derived in gNB RRCenc RRCint UPint UPenc accordance with 5.3.13.3**;
- **Suspend SRB1 and the radio bearers configured for SDT, if any**;
- **For each radio bearer configured for SDT**:
  - **Indicate PDCP suspend to lower layers**;
  - **Re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322**;
- **The procedure ends**.

> ✅ **Note**: This behavior applies specifically when the resume is triggered due to an RNA update (i.e., `resumeCause` is `rna-Update`) and the RRCReject is received. The UE does not attempt to re-initiate the resume immediately but instead sets `pendingRNA-Update` to `true` to indicate that the RNA update needs to be retried later, after the wait timer (T302) expires.
